WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.430
Bend a paperclip slightly, then let go.

2
00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:05.310
It springs straight back.

3
00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:07.800
Bend it further, and let go again.

4
00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:10.050
This time it stays bent.

5
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.090
Same clip, same metal.

6
00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:15.290
Something about it has changed for good.

7
00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:19.540
Why does a small bend spring
back, while a bigger one stays?

8
00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:23.600
In this mission, you'll read a metal
wire's force and extension graph,

9
00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:26.670
from its first straight stretch
to the moment it breaks.

10
00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:31.900
Then you'll pull apart two points on
that graph that most people treat as one.

11
00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:35.400
Your mission: explain why
a small bend springs back,

12
00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:37.250
but a big bend stays.
